.TH "OPS\-DEPLOY" 1 "" "ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ops\-deploy \- ship a service
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBops deploy\fR [flags] <service> [COUNT]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&.ship is not reversible.
.PP
Read the runbook first.
.PP
This command is in beta: it may change in a minor release.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fI<service>\fR
the service to ship
.sp
The service to ship, by its registry name.
.sp
Names are lowercase.
.br
2 to 63 characters; matches \fB^[a\-z][a\-z0\-9\-]*$\fR
.TP
\fI[COUNT]\fR
how many copies
.br
at least 1
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIint\fR
listen port (default 8080)
.sp
The port the service listens on.
.br
between 1 and 65535
.TP
\fB\-\-ratio\fR \fInumber\fR
traffic share (experimental)
.br
greater than 0 and at most 1
.TP
\fB\-\-step\fR \fIint\fR
rollout step
.br
a multiple of 5
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fIstring...\fR
a label
.br
1 to 5 values; each value at most 10 characters; several values per occurrence,
separated by ","; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIduration\fR
how long to wait
.br
at least 1s and less than 1h
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-env\fR \fIkey=value\fR
extra environment
.br
at most 8 values; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fIstring\fR
the deploy token (@file or \- for stdin)
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fIstring\fR
the signing key (@file)
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fIstring...\fR
a label to apply (default ["a,b", "c\e"d"])
.br
several values per occurrence, separated by ","; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-zone\fR \fIstring...\fR
the zones to use (default ["eu", "us"])
.br
repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-quote\fR \fIstring\fR
the quoting style [a\(gab|plain]
.br
matches \fB^[a\-z\(ga"]+$\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-secrets\fR \fIstring\fR
read secrets from this file
.TP
\fB\-\-stage\fR \fIstring\fR
the stage to deploy to
.TP
\fB\-\-sep\fR \fIstring\fR
the field separator
.br
exactly 1 character
.TP
\fB\-\-points\fR \fIint\fR
story points
.br
between 1 and 21
.TP
\fB\-\-weights\fR \fIkey=number\fR
a weight per zone
.br
repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-link\fR \fIvalue\fR
a link to follow
.TP
\fB\-\-pair\fR \fIstring...\fR
exactly two hosts
.br
exactly 2 values; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-replicas\fR \fIint\fR
how many to run (default 1)
.br
between 1 and 100
.br
also set by \fBOPS_DEPLOY_REPLICAS\fR or config key \fBdeploy.replicas\fR
.PP
\-\-token and \-\-key can\(aqt be used together.
.br
\-\-ratio and \-\-step must be used together.
.br
with \-\-zone eu, \-\-port is required and \-\-quote can\(aqt be used.
.br
unless \-\-key is given, \-\-token is required.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
say more
.br
repeat to count: \-vvv
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIstring\fR
when to color (default auto) [auto|always|never]
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
\fBdeploy.registry\fR \fIstring\fR
the registry to push to (in \&.ops.yaml)
.TP
\fBdeploy.retries\fR \fIint\fR
how many times to retry (default 1)
.br
between 0 and 9
.SH FILES
The first file listed that sets a key supplies it.
.TP
\fI\&./secrets.json\fR
or the file \-\-secrets names; profiles under "stages", chosen by \-\-stage
(default dev)
.TP
\fI~/.ops.yaml\fR
A configuration file.
.TP
\fI\&.ops.yaml\fR
in the working directory or the nearest parent holding one
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
shipped
.TP
\fB4\fR (rejected)
the cluster refused it
.br
See \fIhttps://example.com/ops/rejected\fR.
.SH NOTES
Report problems at https://example.com/ops/issues.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBops\fR(1)
